    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n3569" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Arginūsae</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Arginussae</span></b> , ārum,
		f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀργινοῦσαι</span> or
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀργινοῦσσαι</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>three small islands in the
				Ægean Sea</i>, <i>near Lesbos</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">classem ab Arginusis removere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Off. 1, 24, 84</span></i>
			 B. and K.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Arginussae ab Aege IIII. M. passuum distant,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					5, 31, 39, § 140</span></i>
			 Jan.—And in sing.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">circa Arginussam,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					8, 58, 83, § 225</span></i>
			.</div>
